/**
 * Cyrus mod lifecycle sweeps (docs/DOCUMENTATION.md "Cyrus mod lifecycle"). Two sweeps, both
 * INERT by default and each behind its own Setting (admin: /admin/cyrus-mods):
 *
 *  cyrusLifecycleSweep      Setting cyrus_lifecycle_enabled (default "false")
 *    1. signals: turns the Cyrus verdicts the mod-health log read stores (worker/mod-health.ts,
 *       plan.cyrus) into BROKEN / RECOVERED signals and tells the server owner once per break;
 *    2. crash loop: a Cyrus mod installed/updated in the last 20 min on a server whose game keeps
 *       restarting without finishing its start -> read the log since the change, and when the
 *       evidence pins it on that Cyrus mod, switch it off (engine "disable": the jar moves to
 *       /root/.nxeon-mods/disabled, config kept) and notify. Needs ENABLE_REAL_GAMEMODS=1 (or the
 *       sandbox); never for a mod whose disable could delete world content;
 *    3. auto-update: Cyrus mods the owner opted in (ServerMod.autoUpdate = AUTO) move to their
 *       newest finished, published, not-blocked version, only while nobody is online.
 *
 *  cyrusCompatWatchSweep    Setting cyrus_compat_watch_enabled (default "false"),
 *                           cyrus_compat_watch_dry_run (default "true": record + log, tell nobody)
 *    Creator warnings (lib/cyrus/lifecycle/creator.ts): new game version Cyrus can build for,
 *    servers running the mod on a newer version, errors on 2+ servers. One row per (mod, key),
 *    resolved when it no longer applies, in-app once + email at most 2 per creator per week
 *    (and only where the creator's email preference allows, kind cyrus_creator_alert).
 *
 * Every server write goes through the job queue (lib/mods/queue.ts). Never touches a server that
 * has a job queued or running.
