/**
 * Cyrus mods through the shared mods engine (source "cyrus").
 *
 * A Cyrus mod is a Paper plugin jar built by Cyrus (ModBuild, jar stored on the
 * primary under /var/lib/nxeon/modbuilds). Routing its installs through
 * lib/mods/engine.ts — instead of the old direct copy — means the guest state
 * file records exactly which jar Nxeon placed, so the Mods tab can list it,
 * switch it off/on, update it, roll it back and uninstall it like any
 * catalogue plugin (backups, staged write, rollback included).
 *
 * GameMod row: gameFamily "minecraft", source "cyrus", sourceId = the chain's
 * rootBuildId, active=false (never listed in the catalogue/store), created by
 * lib/cyrus-mods/registry.ts. The version placed is CatalogFacts.targetVersionId
 * (a ModBuild id, for update/rollback), else the chain's current version.
